        cuisine='Musakhan (national dish: roast chicken seasoned generously with tangy sumac, caramelized onions, and extra virgin olive oil, baked atop thick Taboon flatbread and garnished with toasted pine nuts), Maqluba ("upside-down" dish of spiced rice, fried cauliflower, eggplant, and chicken layered in a pot and flipped theatrically onto a communal platter), Mansaf, Knafeh Nabulsieh (legendary dessert originating in Nablus: sweet stretchy melted Nabulsi goat cheese covered with shredded pastry dough soaked in orange-blossom sugar syrup and crushed pistachios), Hummus, Falafel, Qidreh (spiced rice and lamb slow-cooked in heavy copper pots inside ancient wood-fired bakery ovens in Hebron), and Za\'atar wild thyme spread with fresh olive oil.',
        festivals=['Palestine National Day (November 15)', 'Christmas in Bethlehem (Manger Square celebrations and midnight mass at the Church of the Nativity, broadcast globally on December 24–25 and January 6–7)', 'Olive Harvest Festival', 'Ramallah Contemporary Dance Festival', 'Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha', 'Easter celebrations in Jerusalem'],
