        dance='Dabke (passionate, energetic national folk line dance performed with shoulder-to-shoulder solidarity, synchronized stomps, and jumps to the beat of the Mijwiz reed pipe and Derbake drum at every festive gathering).',
        art='Tatreez (traditional Palestinian cross-stitch embroidery featuring regional geometric patterns: Cypress tree, Damask rose, Stars of Bethlehem, UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage); olive wood carvings of nativity scenes in Bethlehem; mother-of-pearl craftsmanship; renowned visual artist Sliman Mansour (iconic painting "Camel of Burdens" / Jamal al-Mahamel).',
        architecture='Ancient stone architecture of Jerusalem\'s Old City; Mamluk and Ottoman arched stone houses of Nablus and Hebron; Hisham\'s Palace in Jericho (famous for the breathtaking 8th-century Umayyad mosaic "Tree of Life", one of the largest floor mosaics in the world); Church of the Nativity in Bethlehem (4th-century basilica, UNESCO).',
        literature='Mahmoud Darwish (universally acclaimed national poet: "Identity Card" - Write down! I am an Arab; "Memory for Forgetfulness"); Ghassan Kanafani ("Men in the Sun"); Edward Said ("Orientalism"); Fadwa Tuqan; contemporary author Raja Shehadeh.',
        cinema='Internationally acclaimed cinema; two-time Oscar-nominated director Hany Abu-Assad ("Paradise Now", "Omar"); Elia Suleiman ("Divine Intervention", Cannes Jury Prize; "It Must Be Heaven"); Farah Nabulsi ("The Present", BAFTA winner).',
        sports='Football is an immense national passion (Palestine national football team "The Knights of Palestine" achieved a historic milestone by qualifying for the knockout stages of the AFC Asian Cup in 2024); Running (Palestine Marathon in Bethlehem); Equestrian tent pegging; Street Workout and Parkour in Gaza.',
