        festivals=['Sinulog Festival in Cebu City (third Sunday of January: millions dancing in street processions shouting "Pit Señor!" honoring the Santo Niño)', 'Ati-Atihan Festival in Kalibo, Aklan (ancient tribal dance with soot-covered bodies)', 'Dinagyang Festival in Iloilo', 'Pahiyas Festival in Lucban (decorating houses with colorful translucent rice-wafer sheets / Kiping and fruits)', 'MassKara Festival in Bacolod (joyous street dancing with smiling smiling masks)', 'Panagbenga Flower Festival in Baguio'],
        music='Kundiman (traditional soulful lyric love songs expressing deep longing and patriotism); Kulintang (ancient bronze gong chime ensemble of Mindanao, UNESCO); OPM (Original Pilipino Music - vibrant acoustic ballads, pop, and rock: Eraserheads, Regine Velasquez, SB19 - global P-pop powerhouse); world-class choral traditions (Philippine Madrigal Singers).',
        dance='Tinikling (national folk dance: dancers skip gracefully between two clapping bamboo poles imitating the movements of the Tikling bird); Singkil (regal Maranao royal dance over criss-crossing bamboo poles enacting the Darangen epic, UNESCO); Pandanggo sa Ilaw (balancing oil lamps on heads and hands).',
        art='Spoliarium by Juan Luna (monumental 19th-century masterpiece at the National Museum of the Philippines); Fernando Amorsolo (beloved National Artist famed for glowing pastoral Philippine landscapes); Paete woodcarvings; vibrant contemporary Manila art gallery scene (Art Fair Philippines).',
        architecture='Baroque Churches of the Philippines (UNESCO "Earthquake Baroque" architecture with massive buttresses: San Agustin Church in Intramuros Manila, Miagao Church in Iloilo, Paoay Church in Ilocos Norte, Santa Maria Church); traditional Bahay Kubo (stilt bamboo and nipa hut); Spanish colonial stone mansions (Bahay na Bato) in Vigan; modern glass skyscrapers of Bonifacio Global City (BGC) and Makati.',
        literature='Dr. José Rizal\'s revolutionary masterworks written in Spanish: "Noli Me Tángere" (Touch Me Not) and "El Filibusterismo"; Francisco Balagtas\'s epic poem "Florante at Laura"; Nick Joaquin (National Artist for Literature: "The Woman Who Had Two Navels"); contemporary poetry and fiction by F. Sionil José.',
        cinema='The Golden Ages of Philippine Cinema (Lino Brocka: "Manila in the Claws of Light", Ishmael Bernal: "Himala"); contemporary auteur Lav Diaz (Golden Lion winner at Venice for "The Woman Who Left"); internationally acclaimed director Brillante Mendoza (Cannes Best Director for "Kinatay").',
        sports='Basketball is an absolute national religion (PBA - Philippine Basketball Association is the oldest professional basketball league in Asia; basketball hoops found in every rural barangay); Boxing (Manny Pacquiao - historic eight-division world champion and global sporting legend); Weightlifting (Hidilyn Diaz made history by winning the Philippines\' first-ever Olympic Gold medal at Tokyo 2020); Gymnastics (Carlos Yulo won historic double Olympic Gold medals in floor exercise and vault at Paris 2024); Pole Vault (EJ Obiena, world #2); Billiards (Efren "Bata" Reyes - greatest pool player of all time).',
        media='GMA Network, ABS-CBN (digital and broadcast content powerhouse), TV5, Philippine Daily Inquirer, The Philippine Star, and digital outlets Rappler and Inquirer.net.',
