        internetUsage='99.0% (world-leading 5G speeds, universal adoption of Tawakkalna, Absher, and Nafath digital e-government platforms, and ubiquitous Apple Pay / Mada mobile payments)',
        cuisine='Kabsa / Majboos (national dish: spiced basmati rice slow-cooked in rich meat broth seasoned with black dried lime, cardamom, cloves, cinnamon, and bay leaves, topped with tender lamb, chicken, or camel meat, garnished with toasted almonds and raisins), Mandi (traditional meat and rice slow-cooked in a tandoor pit inside the earth, originating in the south), Jareesh (savory cracked wheat porridge slow-cooked with meat and caramelized onions, designated a national heritage dish), Mutabbaq (crispy folded stuffed pan-fried thin pastry filled with minced meat, eggs, and scallions), Saleeg (creamy white rice cooked in meat broth and milk, served with roasted chicken), and Saudi Coffee (Qahwa) accompanied by premium Sukkari dates and sweet Ma\'amoul pastries.',
