        literature='Ancient pre-Islamic Mu\'allaqat (The Hanging Poems of the Golden Ode, recited at the Souq Okaz near Taif); rich Nabati poetry tradition; modern literature by Abdul Rahman Munif (epic quintet "Cities of Salt"), Ghazi Al-Gosaibi, and Rajaa Alsanea ("Girls of Riyadh").',
        cinema='Rapidly booming cinema and film industry (since lifting the 35-year ban on cinemas in 2018): Red Sea International Film Festival in Jeddah; award-winning Saudi directors Haifaa al-Mansour ("Wadjda", first full-length feature film shot entirely in Saudi Arabia) and contemporary box office smashes.',
        sports='Football is an absolute national passion (Saudi Arabia national team qualified for 6 FIFA World Cups, famously defeating eventual champion Argentina at the 2022 World Cup; Saudi Pro League attracted global icons Cristiano Ronaldo, Neymar, Karim Benzema; hosting the 2027 AFC Asian Cup and 2034 FIFA World Cup); Motorsport (Dakar Rally held across the Saudi desert, Formula 1 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix in Jeddah); Horse Racing (The Saudi Cup - world\'s richest horse race with a $20 million purse at King Abdulaziz Racetrack); Falconry; Camel Racing.',
        media='Saudi Press Agency (SPA), Arab News (premier English daily), Asharq Al-Awsat (influential pan-Arab newspaper), Okaz, Al Riyadh, MBC Group (largest media conglomerate in the Arab world, headquartered in Riyadh), and Al Arabiya news channel.',
        clothing='Men wear the Thobe (crisp white in summer, dark wool in winter) paired with the red-and-white checkered Shemagh or white Gutra held by the black Agal, and for formal events the gold-trimmed ceremonial Bisht / Mishlah; women wear fashionable Abayas in diverse colors, paired with the Hijab or modern haute couture; regional traditional attire celebrated on Founding Day: Al-Dahma, Al-Majdal, and Al-Khabba.',
