        flagDescription='A green rectangular field (representing Islam) bearing the Arabic inscription of the Shahada ("There is no god but Allah; Muhammad is the messenger of Allah") in white Thuluth script, situated above a horizontal white scimitar / sword pointing to the hoist (symbolizing the sword of King Abdulaziz and justice); the flag is never flown at half-mast, even in times of national mourning, out of reverence for the sacred creed.',
        coatOfArmsDescription='Two crossed silver scimitars in saltire beneath a golden date palm tree, with the palm tree symbolizing vitality, growth, and prosperity, and the crossed swords symbolizing justice, strength, and national defense.',
