        flagDescription='A golden-yellow field featuring a dark red/maroon rectangle containing a golden lion passant holding a Kastane sword in its right forepaw (symbolizing the Sinhalese nation and courage), with four golden bo tree leaves in the four corners (symbolizing the four Buddhist virtues: loving-kindness, compassion, sympathetic joy, and equanimity); on the hoist side are two vertical stripes of green (representing Muslim Sri Lankans) and orange (representing Tamil Sri Lankans), all enclosed by a yellow border (The Lion Flag).',
        coatOfArmsDescription='The national emblem features a golden lion holding a sword in a circle surrounded by golden lotus petals, resting on a traditional grain vase (Punkalasa) overflowing with sheaves of rice, topped by the blue Dharmachakra wheel of law, flanked by the sun and moon.',
        symbols={'animal': 'Sri Lankan elephant and Lion (heraldic)', 'bird': 'Sri Lanka junglefowl (Gallus lafayettii)', 'tree': 'Ceylon ironwood (Na tree / Mesua ferrea)', 'flower': 'Blue water lily (Nil Mahanel / Nymphaea nouchali)', 'sport': 'Volleyball'},
        landmarks=['Sigiriya Rock Fortress (Lion Rock ancient palace citadel)', 'Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic (Kandy)', 'Galle Dutch Fort and Lighthouse', 'Nine Arch Bridge and Ella tea plantation gap', 'Dambulla Golden Cave Temple (ancient Buddhist murals)', 'Yala National Park (leopard safari)', 'Adam\'s Peak / Sri Pada (sacred sunrise mountain)', 'Ruwanwelisaya and Jaya Sri Maha Bodhi (Anuradhapura)', 'Mirissa whale watching bay'],
        travelNotes='Extremely welcoming, scenic, and budget-friendly island; electronic travel authorization (ETA) / tourist visa available online; scenic train ride between Kandy and Ella is considered one of the most beautiful train journeys in the world; credit cards widely accepted in hotels and restaurants in Colombo and Galle, while cash (LKR) is useful for rural tuk-tuks and local tea shops; tap water should be avoided in favor of filtered/bottled water.',
